      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "$$\nC=[-1,1],\\,D={n<5∣\\,n\\in N}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $C$ and $D$ (given above):",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinalities of two sets cannot be equal if one set is finite and the other is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, notice that \n\n- $C$ is infinite (since it's an interval of real numbers), while\n\n- $D={1,2,3,4}$ is finite with $|D|=4,$ .\n\nTherefore, $|C|\\ne |D|.$",
